			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Finalize PascalCase migration and update smoke test paths\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to complete the strict PascalCase directory hierarchy migration across six core components (Cocoon, Output, Mountain, Sky, Common, Wind) and adjust the integration smoke test scripts to reflect new artifact paths.\n\nThe Element update restructures the Cocoon source tree, aligns Output's ESBuild pipeline, extends Mountain's IPC timeouts to 5000ms for cold-boot stability, and activates dormant Tauri event relays in Sky. Concurrently, Maintain/Integration/SmokeProfiles.sh is updated to reference the relocated `Cocoon/Main.js` bundle, ensuring the verification suite correctly detects the new build artifacts.\n\nThese changes eliminate module resolution failures in the Tauri environment, prevent startup freezes, and ensure build diagnostics accurately reflect the current codebase structure.",
			"SHA": "4bbae8eb7cb049307fc5d0966f493e4486947400"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:43:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Update Wind dependencies and CI action versions\n\nSynchronize the Element submodule to update the Wind component's GitHub Actions and Tauri plugin dependencies. Upgrade `pnpm/action-setup` from v6.0.3 to v6.0.5 and bump `@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog` from v2.7.0 to v2.7.1.\n\nThese updates ensure the extension host service layer aligns with the latest upstream patch versions for build tooling and native dialog support, maintaining compatibility with the current release channel.",
			"SHA": "7ead71f73211cb9b2e526266bd7767037f01195d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:40:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Enforce PascalCase hierarchy and remove legacy artifacts\n\nUpdate the Element submodule to reorganize the core component submodules (Cocoon, Output, Sky, Wind) into a strict nested PascalCase directory hierarchy. Migrate extension host modules, build pipelines, and workbench sources to new paths (e.g., `Type/Converter.ts`) while updating all import references to prevent Tauri/WKWebView resolution errors.\n\nConcurrently purge deprecated `*Upstream.ts` and `*BridgeShapeGenerated.ts` artifacts from Wind to clear dependencies on the previous VS Code sync and enable the new Common/Mountain contract generation workflow. These content-preserving structural changes align the entire codebase with project naming conventions and enhance navigability.",
			"SHA": "b3f6fb7ec64590e71d5a7a5e63c694107427fced"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T17:27:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize submodules to restore extension webview asset loading and stabilize rendering\n\nUpdate four core submodules to resolve critical failures where popular extensions (e.g., Roo, GitLens) failed to render assets due to WebKit Service Worker restrictions on custom protocols.\n\nCocoon implements asWebviewUri to translate legacy VS Code URI schemes into the native vscode-file scheme, bypassing Service Worker requirements. Mountain registers asynchronous handlers for legacy schemes and enforces Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy headers to satisfy WebKit COEP security policies. Output introduces PatchWebviewIframeServiceWorker to disable registration checks causing bootstrap hangs and adds a global port capture hook for message port recovery. Sky normalizes formatting for consistency.\n\nThese changes bridge the gap between VS Code's URI handling and Tauri's custom protocol implementation, ensuring extension sidebars and webview panels render correctly without hanging.",
			"SHA": "1f2ee49e95f04c4fe991bea18cbdad7ef43df6e2"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-04T15:10:28Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				116,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize submodules to resolve webview hangs and race conditions\n\nUpdate four core submodules to address critical UI stalls in extension webviews and restore deterministic rendering behavior. Output patches the ESBuild pipeline to disable ServiceWorkers on Tauri/WKWebView custom protocols and short-circuits extension activation deadlocks for `onView` events. Cocoon refactors all Webview RPC handlers to use named-key payloads, eliminating reliance on positional argument mapping. Sky implements a real `WebviewInput` integration with a pending HTML cache to replay synchronous HTML assignments that previously occurred before resolver registration.\n\nThese changes ensure extension sidebars and webview panels render correctly without hanging on the chrome shell, while strengthening IPC payload safety against future Rust-side refactors.",
			"SHA": "73c01c9831d2b56f7c1bfb55397b4ba2f426864d"
		}
	],
